    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen viewing a file in nvim (e.g. `some_dir/some_file.txt`) and then deleting that file's parent directory via another process (e.g. `git rm -r some_dir`), nvim becomes unresponsive, repeatedly showing the following in the message area:\n\n```lua\nLua callback:\nC:/Program Files/Neovim/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/log.lua:107: attempt to index local 'info' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        C:/Program Files/Neovim/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/log.lua:107: in function 'format_func'\n        C:/Program Files/Neovim/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/log.lua:236: in function <C:/Program Files/Neovim/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/log.lua:228>\n```\n\nThis was using NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1583+gd039f19af5.  Using a prior build (v0.13.0-dev-1572+g318ea4de21), the result was the same but the error was in ..share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_watch.lua and contained `EPERM` (sorry, didn't save the error /call stack).\n\nIf only the file is removed, but not it's parent directory, nvim displays the more familiar `E211: File \"some_dir/somefile.txt\" no longer available` and is still responsive.\n\nMight be related to issue #32386? And I believe the error changed (from somewhere in `_watch.lua` to `log.lua`)  when pr #41776 was merged.\n\nP.S. If you enable `:h ui2`, you don't have to kill the nvim process; you are able to exit normally.\n\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create a directory, create a file in that directory (e.g. `~/some_dir` and `~/some_dir/some_file.txt`)\n2. open the file in nvim (`nvim --clean .\\some_dir\\some_file.txt`)\n3. in another terminal pane delete the directory (`rm -r .\\some_dir`)\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nnvim displays the same message as when just the file (not it's whole parent directory) is removed by another process: `E211: File \"some_dir/somefile.txt\" no longer available`\n\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1583+gd039f19af5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nna\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal Preview / 1.25.1912.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nna\n\n### Installation\n\ndownload nvim-win64.zip from releases",
