            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I took a look at this issue today, seems it's libuv bug that happens to be exposed by the per-file watcher in #37971. This bug affects a lot of libuv consumers 😅 (node, vscode, bun, webpack, etc.)\n\nOn Windows, file watcher actually watches the file's parent directory. If that directory is permanently deleted, libuv re-arms `ReadDirectoryChangesW` on the dead handle, producing an endless stream of `UV_EPERM` error callbacks (~270k/s measured). [libuv#4376](https://github.com/libuv/libuv/pull/4376) and [libuv#5013](https://github.com/libuv/libuv/pull/5013) only cover **directory** watchers, the file-watch path still spins at libuv HEAD.\n\nI see there's also mention [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40238#issuecomment-4845785953) of wanting to switch to per-directory. The hang can be pretty annoying once it happens, not sure if we still want to use a temporary workaround for this issue, e.g.\n```diff\ndiff --git a/runtime/lua/vim/_watch.lua b/runtime/lua/vim/_watch.lua\nindex 3e10e179a0..1d5b07cb1f 100644\n--- a/runtime/lua/vim/_watch.lua\n+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/_watch.lua\n@@ -451,6 +451,9 @@ local function watch(path, opts, callback)\n     if events.rename then\n       local _, staterr, staterrname = uv.fs_stat(fullpath)\n       if staterrname == 'ENOENT' then\n+        if is_win and not watching_dir then\n+          handle:stop()\n+        end\n         change_type = M.FileChangeType.Deleted\n       else\n         if staterr then\n```",
