        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> About the suggested workaround above - it looks too broad, ENOENT for a child when watching a directory will stop the whole directory watcher. If pursuing the workaround approach, that should probably be narrowed down to file watchers only, and on Windows only.\n\nchanged to `if is_win and not watching_dir then`\n\n>  sure, what's the worse case risk?\n\nI don't see much of risk.\nFor `autoread`, we're just executing `handle:stop` immediately instead of delaying it through the debounce, and it can be called multiple times.\nFor LSP, seems that servers generally watch directories, so this shouldn't affect them either.",
